// @run
// @log 3
// THE KIND-9 LEAF — the 3-D twin of `nested-array-inferred-empty-unsupported-leaf.vl`, where
// the "leaf" is itself an ARRAY. It pinned a loud `index receiver is not an array or string`;
// D702 makes it run, and it is the leg that proves the harder half of that change.
//
// The old divergence: the arena said kind 4 (the i32-list wrapper) while the name said kind 9
// (the inner row's own wrapper). Its header called the fix "not a wider guard but a real design
// step, because kind 9 reads `rlWrapIdx[rlElemInnerSlot(rs)]` during the same forward pass, so
// the inner row has to be interned at a strictly lower slot index than the outer" — and that is
// exactly what the change does: the kind-9 arm of `collectA` interns through `ensureRefElemTy`,
// the annotated path's own inner-first DRY core, instead of calling `rlInternNameTy` flat.
//
// Interning flat is not a theoretical hazard. Built that way first, `const c = [[[1, 2]]]` was
// `vl check` rc 0 and `type mismatch: expected (ref null $type), found (ref $type)` at load —
// the outer backing typed from a row whose inner wrapper did not exist yet.
function deepLeaf() {
  const outer = []
  const mid = [[1, 2, 3]]
  outer.push(mid)
  print(outer[0][0][2])
}
deepLeaf()
